---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  title="About"
  description="leesun — M.Eng. candidate in Software Engineering at USTC, working on LLM applications, agents and RAG."
  pathname="/en/about/"
>
  <div class="container">
    <article class="prose">
      <header class="page-head">
        <h1>About</h1>
      </header>

      <p>
        I'm leesun. I did my B.Eng. in Computer Science at Shantou University (STU), and I'm now
        an M.Eng. candidate in Software Engineering at USTC, working on LLM applications, agents
        and RAG. I write code, read papers, and keep algorithm notes here.
      </p>

      <p>
        The site is called 自留地 — "the plot you keep for yourself." No recommendation feed, no
        ads, no chasing whatever is trending. Only the things I want to come back to.
      </p>

      <h2>What I'm working on</h2>

      <p>
        Right now, LLM applications: wiring retrieval, tool use and multi-step reasoning into
        systems that actually run rather than staying at the demo stage. I also maintain
        <a href="/en/projects/paste/">Paste</a>, a native macOS clipboard manager — my answer to
        the question of how light a small utility should be.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>Email: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a></li>
        <li>GitHub: <a href={SITE.github} rel="me noreferrer">github.com/leesun1729</a></li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* global.css ships .wrap (896px, centered) and BaseLayout applies it to
     <main>. The promised .container utility was not implemented there, so
     pages that need it define it locally rather than editing global.css. */

  .page-head {
    padding-block: 28px;
  }
</style>
